WEBVTT

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.610
Okay.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.980
Look, it's done.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.380
Yamauchi Temple

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.260
Okay, is everyone ready?

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.740
Ready, go!

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.910
Anyone home!?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.030
Everyone, welcome to my home.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.360
I Want to Meet the Ghost!

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.710
Wow.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.540
I'm feeling kind of nervous.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.880
They all look so stern.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.130
Well then, shall we start?

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.680
I can't wait!

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:46.220
The last story of summer vacation is about a master of a temple.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.810
Yamauchi's stories are the best.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.690
Summer vacation is a waste without hearing this.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:52.610
What kind of story is it?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.320
That master's daughter just passed away.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.490
Every day, he would visit his daughter's grave.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:06.450
One day, he saw a little girl.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:13.880
And on the next day, that same girl was still there, standing in the rain without an umbrella.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.760
What are you doing here?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.510
I'm waiting for someone.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:24.260
I promised my father that I would wait here until he finishes his work.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.850
You promised him...?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.020
After that, the girl did not answer any more of the man's questions.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:34.940
Why?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.520
Stop askin' questions and jus' listen.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:43.240
Every day, he would see that girl standing there with the same solemn expression.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:49.700
Gradually, that man started to think about how to make that girl smile.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:56.340
But no matter what he said, the girl's expression never changed.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.210
Couldn't he just tell something like an old man's joke?

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.550
But bad old man jokes would just make her even more depressed.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.760
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.300
You guys would know!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.510
This continued for some time, until...

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.620
Mister!

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.100
Thank you for all that you've done.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.960
I can finally see my father tomorrow.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.980
Ohh? That's so wonderful!

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:20.780
Yep!

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:27.740
As he saw that girl's smile, he too, felt great joy inside.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.740
All is well, all is well.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:31.950
That's it?

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.750
I think it was missin' somethin'...

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.250
No way...

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.750
It was a great story.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.840
Actually...

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.710
There is an epilogue to this story.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.010
I knew it!

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.970
You sure know how to tell stories.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.350
Many days passed after that.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.850
Did something happen to that little girl?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.940
Little girl?

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.190
The one who passed away was my husband.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:08.070
In front of the grave, he saw a picture of that little girl, smiling.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:14.000
The deceased doctor had a daughter who passed away when she was very young.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.670
Doctor, it's an emergency!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.680
I'm sorry, can you call another doctor?

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.550
Father...

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.920
Go.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.380
But...

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.680
I'm fine...

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.470
Please save those patients...

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:35.350
I will wait here until you finish your work.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.770
It's a promise.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.100
I understand.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.200
I'll be right back.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:42.860
Okay.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:52.410
But the doctor did not get a chance to see his daughter again.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.160
I promise you...

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.340
I will work even harder than before...

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:07.590
Following his promise, the father saved countless patients.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.760
And the girl always waited until her father finished his work.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.610
So scary!

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.100
H-Hadzuki-chan?

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.650
Well, that girl's a ghost, right!?

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.560
She was waiting for her father, right!?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.860
You're the one that's scary.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.150
It's a good story.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.280
No, no, no, no, noooooo!!!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.490
Fujiwara, there's someone behind you.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.960
No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:33.370
Nooooooo!!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.540
There's something on your right shoulder.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.720
Nooooooooooo!!!!!!!!

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.080
Now it's above you!

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.420
No... more...

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.300
It'd be better if you didn't lean against that pillar.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.760
There's someone there.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.550
Someone?

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.560
Yamauchi-kun's words are definitely the scariest.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:06.190
That's our Yada-kun, so calm even when everyone's like this.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.490
Can't move... my legs.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.530
No, no...

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.120
After hearing that story, how can I go on a test of courage?

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.870
It's more fun after hearing that story.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.250
I promise you that there won't be any ghosts.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.420
What a pain.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.480
Oh yeah.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:30.330
Hadzuki-chan, if yer really that scared, just think of Majo Rika.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.430
Majo Rika?

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:35.260
Yep! If ya think of her, then the ghosts'll be much cuter in comparison!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.660
Yep.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.560
Her cruel heart is more evil than any ghost.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.520
And she's a Witch Frog, on top of all that.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.110
Yeah.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.400
You'll be fine.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.710
Yeah, I'm feeling braver than earlier.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.610
That's right, if yer scared, just think of Majo Rika.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.410
Okay.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.950
Are you okay?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.410
Someone's talking about me.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.160
It's so nice being popular.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.170
I think it's a cold.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.670
Okay? Don't back out.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.380
Have a nice trip!

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.630
We'll be going now...

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:20.810
We are the hilarious three-man team!

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.520
Did you just hear something?

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.730
Y-You're imagining things.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.440
N-No... I really did hear something.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.190
Shall we take a look?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.330
We saw it!

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.920
A real ghost!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.840
Their new act?

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.050
It's not very funny.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.460
It's true!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.170
We really saw a ghost of a floating grandpa!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.720
I don't think they are lying.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:09:00.430
You two probably saw my father's father.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.260
Your father's father? Your grandfather?

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:08.940
Yes, he passed away two years ago, but he has yet to reach nirvana.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:16.110
My housekeeper has also seen him many times, but for some reason he has never appeared before me.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.240
This is a great scoop!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.740
I'll take a good picture of him with my camera!

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.410
I want to interview him.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.000
Things sure have gotten complicated.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.380
Majo Rika, Majo Rika...

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.290
This is too scary.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:39.050
And now, the story of Boy Detective Tatekawa reaches its final chapter!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:39.730
Really?

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:42.600
There will be a magnificent, tear-jerking ending!

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.060
I hope you look forward to it!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:44.480
Yeah!

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.980
We saw it! A very scary one.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.440
No lie?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:55.490
While Ai-chan and I were walking together, tightly holding each other,

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.610
I heard a sound from beyond the grave!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.910
And then?

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:01.950
There was an old man with white hair and a very long neck...

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.080
There wasn't, there wasn't.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.080
That won't do, Ai-chan, you have to be more persuasive.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:10.170
I understand how ya feel about it, but the next pair is...

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.750
Majo Rika, Majo Rika, Majo Rika,

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.220
Hey! Fujiwara, what on earth are you yelling about!?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.590
What's "Majo Rika?"

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.570
Ah, it's a spell.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.100
Ai-chan taught me to say it whenever I'm scared.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.810
Does it work? That spell?

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.860
Yes, because I don't feel as scared when I say it.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:31.690
Really?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.320
Did... Did you feel something just now?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.700
Don't look at it.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.240
Majo Rikaaaaaaaa!

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.290
Majo Rika, Majo Rika,

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.620
Shut up!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.620
Go to sleep!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.960
Sorry.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.380
Looks like ya both made it in one piece.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.850
It's all thanks to Ai-chan's spell.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:01.890
Now it's my turn.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.350
Aren't you afraid, Doremi-chan?

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.730
But didn't Yamauchi-kun already say that a ghost wouldn't appear?

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.350
It's because I'm in the same group as Yamauchi-kun.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.420
Yamauchi-kun?

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.260
You're walking too fast.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.010
Sorry.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:50.940
These graves sure look scary at night.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:53.400
We'll be fine.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.070
A ghost won't appear when I'm around anyway.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.820
Yamauchi-kun?

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.910
Don't tell me you want to see your grandfather's ghost?

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:08.870
I need to apologize to him.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.120
When my grandfather passed away, I said some terrible things to him.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:19.260
Grandpa... Grandpa...

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.630
I hate you so much!

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:26.680
If I could meet him, even if he's a ghost, then I could apologize.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:32.310
As a child of a temple, it's not becoming of me to talk about such matters.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.730
They're back.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.570
Hey, you made it.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.990
Are you okay?

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.190
Somewhat.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.530
You two, come with me for a second.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.160
We need to use the restroom.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:48.160
Let's go.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.370
What the?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.090
I see.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.400
So that's what happened to Yamauchi-kun.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:01.630
Now that ya mention it, he looked pretty sad when he was talkin' about his grandfather.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:03.010
Can we do anything?

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.470
Alright! Let's give it a try!

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.220
Magical Stage, right?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.930
Wait a second!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:12.390
You want to call up his grandfather's ghost using magic?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.690
No way, Hadzuki-chan.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.580
Yeah...

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.400
There's no other way.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.280
Hadzuki-chan!

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.070
We're helping others this way!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.070
She's right!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.080
Is she okay?

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.000
Hadzuki-chan, we're starting.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.500
Okay-Okay.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.250
Pirika Pirilala Carefreely!

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:46.220
Paipai-Ponpoi-Flexibly!

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.310
Pameruku Laruku Proudly!

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.400
Magical Stage!

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.450
It's a scoop! A scoop!

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:19.580
Let Yamauchi-kun see his grandfather's ghost!

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.220
A horse?

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.180
We saw it! We saw it! We saw it!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.990
This time, something on the other side of the grave let out some strange light!

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:38.890
Yamauchi!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.730
Okay, let's go after them!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.940
You guys are such cowards.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.110
What does this horse have to do with anything?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.690
Yamauchi-kun, what's wrong?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:56.910
The others say they saw a strange light around here.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.620
W-We didn't see anything.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:00.170
Nope!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:00.750
Yeah yeah!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.670
T-That's...

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.910
Where did you find this?

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:08.670
Um...

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.510
Oh yeah, it came falling from the sky.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:14.010
It was probably hangin' from a tree.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:14.720
Yeah yeah!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:16.560
Is that so?

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.200
This is pretty cool.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:32.990
Yeah!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.330
There are so many wood carvings.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.580
They were all made by my grandfather.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.290
And that horse too?

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.750
I grew up at my grandpa's side.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:50.800
Because my parents were so busy, my grandfather always played with me.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.550
Grandpa!

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.560
What are you making?

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.230
Look.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:02.850
It's a horse!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.560
I'll give it to you when I'm done.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.230
Really?

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.530
Have I ever lied to you?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.270
Nope, never.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:16.630
Okay, I should be done when you come back from school.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:17.760
Get going now.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.000
Okay, I'm going now!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.160
It's a promise!

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:24.250
You must finish it!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.170
Okay, I promise.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.010
But my grandpa...

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.390
Didn't you promise me...

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.600
That you'd finish it when I came home?

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.900
Didn't we promise!?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:53.240
Grandpa... Grandpa...

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.160
I hate you so much!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.620
This was that horse.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.050
So that's why it ain't finished.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:02.660
Yes.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.160
But...

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.220
Why would that wood carving come falling down in the first place?

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:11.050
If we knew that, then maybe we could meet his grandfather.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.090
That's impossible.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.420
My grandfather never forgave me.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.800
Because I said those mean things...

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.060
That's not true!

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:23.890
Then why has he not appeared before me!?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.270
That's...

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.570
I'm sorry... I raised my voice.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.580
Can you go ahead and head back without me?

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:33.690
But...

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:34.610
Doremi-chan.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.100
Okay, we'll go back first.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.030
I'm sorry...

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:45.710
Grandpa...

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:48.750
Why...

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.420
Why won't you appear?

00:17:55.510 --> 00:18:00.470
Shinshuu...

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.650
Grandpa.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.190
Long time no see.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.110
Why...

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.610
Why?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:22.830
Why wasn't I able to see you these last two years!?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.580
I was always waiting!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.620
I wanted...

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.120
I wanted to apologize!

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.880
I said some terrible things.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.300
I'm so sorry.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:40.930
I'm so sorry...

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:44.810
I'm the one who's supposed to apologize.

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:49.310
If I had kept my promise, then this wouldn't have happened.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.770
So it was because of my promise...

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:55.030
That's not it.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:59.150
I really wanted to fulfill our promise.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:04.370
I wanted to finish that horse, so I went around looking for help.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:08.080
But when people saw me, they ran.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.500
Well, that's the obvious reaction.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.960
I wouldn't have been scared.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.630
Please teach me.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.930
I will finish this horse.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.730
Like this?

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.560
Ah, I see.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.560
I see. Okay, I got it.

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.230
Is he talking to himself?

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.320
Can we do anything for him?

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:45.490
I got it!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:49.300
If that's the case, let's turn into his grandfather's ghost.

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:51.460
Oh, that's a good idea.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.750
Okay.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.130
What are you doing?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:54.710
Nothing!

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.040
Shimakura-san!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.050
What is it?

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.920
W-W-W-W-W-W-When we went to the restroom, we got lost.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.590
You guys are weird.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.260
Mind your own business.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:06.390
Speaking of weird things, Yamauchi-kun is also acting weird.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:11.960
He seems to be making something while talking to himself.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:14.910
It's like someone else is with him, talking to him.

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.190
Isn't that weird?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.700
I'm done, Grandpa.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.700
Thank you, Shinshuu.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.620
Looks like I finally kept my promise.

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.330
Grandpa...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.210
Please don't go yet.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.170
I still have so many things to talk about!

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:43.720
I want you to teach me so many things!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:49.570
I want to be with you longer!

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:50.890
I am here.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:57.560
I will always be by your side.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.480
Grandpa.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.530
Is that a promise?

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.490
Yes, it's a promise.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:16.000
It's a promise, Grandpa.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.360
Thank you.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.210
Eh? What?

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.300
I heard something.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:33.560
Was that... Yamauchi-kun's grandfather just now?

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.980
But it wasn't scary at all.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:36.980
Yeah.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.360
He seemed very kind.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:53.660
It's also a bright day today, Grandpa.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:07.110
Hey, hey, Shino-chan from our class received a present from a friend in Mongolia.

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:10.640
Yep, and she doesn't know what to give back in return.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:13.160
Mongolia is a place fulla grassy plains, right?

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:14.870
What kinda presents do kids over there like?

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:16.980
This is pretty tough.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.630
What would you give her, Doremi-chan?

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:20.680
Steak, of course!

00:22:20.680 --> 00:22:23.960
We didn't ask you what you want, Doremi-chan.

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:25.040
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:26.930
Presents From Mongolia.

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:29.550
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
